==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|de|Autismus}}, [[Appendix:Glossary#coinage|coined]] by Swiss psychiatrist {{w|Eugen Bleuler}}, first usage dated to 1907 attributed by {{w|Carl Jung}} as an alternative of his for "auto-erotism",<ref>{{cite-book|author=Sigmund Freud|authorlink=Sigmund Freud|author2=Carl Jung|author2link= Carl Jung|editor= William McGuire|translators= Ralph Manheim, R.F.C. Hull|title= The Freud/Jung Letters|archivedate= 2018-02-26 09:36:34|edition= 1st|location= Princeton, New Jersey|publisher= Princeton University Press|year= 1974|section= 24j|pages= 44-5|pageurl= https://archive.org/details/FreudJungLetters/page/n85/mode/2up?view=theater|isbn= 0691098905|text= Bleuler still misses a clear definition of autoerotism and its specifically psychological effects. He has, however, accepted the concept for his Dem. pr. contribution to Aschaffenburg’s Handbook. He doesn't want to say autoerotism (for reasons we all know), but prefers “autism” or “ipsism.” I have already got accustomed to “autoerotism.”}}</ref> although Bleuler himself differentiates the terms in his book ''Dementia Praecox'', first published 1911.<ref>{{cite-book|author= Paul Eugen Bleuler|authorlink= Eugen Bleuler|chapter= 1|editor= Gustav Aschaffenburg|title= Dementia Praecox oder Gruppe der Schizophrenien|trans-title= Dementia Praecox or the Group of Schizophrenias|url= https://iiif.wellcomecollection.org/pdf/b21296157|archiveurl= https://archive.org/details/b21296157|archivedate= 2015-04-24 08:07:00.206331|location= Leipzig and Vienna|publisher= Franz Deuticke|year= 1911|section=B.α|page= 52|pageurl= https://archive.org/details/b21296157/page/52/mode/2up?view=theater}}</ref> From {{der|en|grc|αὐτός||self|sc=polytonic}} + {{m|grc|-ισμός||-ism}}.<ref>{{R:Etymonline}}</ref>

